      "text": "To convert from spherical coordinates \\((\\rho, \\theta, \\phi)\\) to rectangular coordinates \\((x, y, z)\\), we use the following formulas:\n\\[\nx = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta\n\\]\n\\[\ny = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta\n\\]\n\\[\nz = \\rho \\cos \\phi\n\\]\n\nGiven the spherical coordinates \\((\\rho, \\theta, \\phi) = \\left( 3, \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, 0 \\right)\\), we can substitute these values into the formulas.\n\nFirst, we calculate \\(x\\):\n\\[\nx = 3 \\sin 0 \\cos \\left( \\frac{5 \\pi}{12} \\right)\n\\]\nSince \\(\\sin 0 = 0\\), we have:\n\\[\nx = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\cos \\left( \\frac{5 \\pi}{12} \\right) = 0\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(y\\):\n\\[\ny = 3 \\sin 0 \\sin \\left( \\frac{5 \\pi}{12} \\right)\n\\]\nSince \\(\\sin 0 = 0\\), we have:\n\\[\ny = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\sin \\left( \\frac{5 \\pi}{12} \\right) = 0\n\\]\n\nFinally, we calculate \\(z\\):\n\\[\nz = 3 \\cos 0\n\\]\nSince \\(\\cos 0 = 1\\), we have:\n\\[\nz = 3 \\cdot 1 = 3\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the rectangular coordinates corresponding to the spherical coordinates \\((3, \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, 0)\\) are:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(0, 0, 3)}\n\\]",
