      "text": "Given the point in spherical coordinates, $(\\rho, \\theta, \\phi) = \\left( 3, \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, 0 \\right)$, we can convert it to rectangular coordinates using the following formulas:\n\n\\[\nx = \\rho \\sin(\\phi) \\cos(\\theta)\n\\]\n\\[\ny = \\rho \\sin(\\phi) \\sin(\\theta)\n\\]\n\\[\nz = \\rho \\cos(\\phi)\n\\]\n\nSubstituting $\\rho = 3$, $\\theta = \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}$, and $\\phi = 0$ into the formula for $\\phi$, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\phi = \\sin(0) = 0\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute the values into the formulas for $x$, $y$, and $z$:\n\n\\[\nx = 3 \\sin(0) \\cos\\left(\\frac{5 \\pi}{12}\\right) = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\cos\\left(\\frac{5 \\pi}{12}\\right) = 0\n\\]\n\\[\ny = 3 \\sin(0) \\sin\\left(\\frac{5 \\pi}{12}\\right) = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\sin\\left(\\frac{5 \\pi}{12}\\right) = 0\n\\]\n\\[\nz = 3 \\cos(0) = 3 \\cdot 1 = 3\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the rectangular coordinates of the given point are:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{(0, 0, 3)}\n\\]",
