      "text": "To convert the given point \\((\\rho, \\theta, \\phi) = \\left( 3, \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, 0 \\right)\\) from spherical coordinates to rectangular coordinates, we use the following transformation formulas:\n\n\\[\nx = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta\n\\]\n\\[\ny = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta\n\\]\n\\[\nz = \\rho \\cos \\phi\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\rho = 3, \\quad \\theta = \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, \\quad \\phi = 0\n\\]\n\nFirst, let's calculate \\(x\\):\n\\[\nx = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta = 3 \\sin 0 \\cos \\left( \\frac{5\\pi}{12} \\right)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 0 = 0 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\cos \\left( \\frac{5\\pi}{12} \\right) = \\cos \\left( \\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{12} \\right) = -\\cos \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{12} \\right)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 0 = 0 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\cos \\left( \\frac{5\\pi}{12} \\right) = -\\cos \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{12} \\right)\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\left( -\\cos \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{12} \\right) \\right) = 0\n\\]\n\nNext, let's calculate \\(y\\):\n\\[\ny = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta = 3 \\sin 0 \\sin \\left( \\frac{5\\pi}{12} \\right)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 0 = 0 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\sin \\left( \\frac{5\\pi}{12} \\right) = \\sin \\left( \\pi - \\frac{7\\pi}{12} \\right) = \\sin \\left( \\frac{7\\pi}{12} \\right)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 0 = 0 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\sin \\left( \\frac{7\\pi}{12} \\right) \\text{ is not zero}\n\\]\n\\[\ny = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\sin \\left( \\frac{7\\pi}{12} \\right) = 0\n\\]\n\nFinally, let's calculate \\(z\\):\n\\[\nz = \\rho \\cos \\phi = 3 \\cos 0 = 3 \\cdot 1 = 3\n\\]\n\nPutting it all together, the rectangular coordinates are:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(0, 0, 3)}\n\\]",
