      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To convert the given point \\((\\rho, \\theta, \\phi) = \\left(3, \\frac{5\\pi}{12}, 0\\right)\\) from spherical coordinates to rectangular (Cartesian) coordinates \\((x, y, z)\\), we use the following relationships between spherical and Cartesian coordinates:\n\n\\[\nx = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta\n\\]\n\\[\ny = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta\n\\]\n\\[\nz = \\rho \\cos \\phi\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\rho = 3, \\quad \\theta = \\frac{5\\pi}{12}, \\quad \\phi = 0\n\\]\n\nFirst, we need to find \\(\\sin \\phi\\), \\(\\cos \\phi\\), \\(\\sin \\theta\\), and \\(\\cos \\theta\\).\n\n\\[\n\\phi = 0 \\implies \\sin \\phi = \\sin 0 = 0, \\quad \\cos \\phi = \\cos 0 = 1\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\nx = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta = 3 \\sin 0 \\cos \\frac{5\\pi}{12}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 0 = 0 \\implies x = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\cos \\frac{5\\pi}{12} = 0\n\\]\n\nNow, we calculate \\(y\\):\n\n\\[\ny = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta = 3 \\sin 0 \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 0 = 0 \\implies y = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12} = 0\n\\]\n\nFinally, we calculate \\(z\\):\n\n\\[\nz = \\rho \\cos \\phi = 3 \\cos 0\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos 0 = 1 \\implies z = 3 \\cdot 1 = 3\n\\]\n\nThus, the rectangular coordinates corresponding to the point \\((\\rho, \\theta, \\phi) = \\left(3, \\frac{5\\pi}{12}, 0\\right)\\) are:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{(0, 0, 3)}\n\\]",
